Diffraction Modulation Transfer Function

Diffraction MTF is a wave-optics calculation for which the only variables (for a given aperture shape) are the aperture diameter D , wavelength λ, and focal length f . The MTF diffraction is the upper limit to the system’s performance; the effects of optical aberrations are assumed to be negligible. Aberrations increase the spot size and thus contribute to a poorer MTF . The diffraction MTF is based on the overall limiting aperture of the system (the aperture stop). The diffraction effects are only calculated once per system and do not accumulate multiplicatively on an element-by-element basis.
Calculation of diffraction MTF

